<title>UK: HORSE RACING-GOODWOOD CUP RESULT.</title>
<headline>HORSE RACING-GOODWOOD CUP RESULT.</headline>
<dateline>GOODWOOD, England 1997-07-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Result of the Goodwood</p>
<p>Cup, a group two race for three-year-olds and upwards, run over</p>
<p>two miles (3.2 km) on Thursday:</p>
<p> 1. Double Trigger   16-1 (ridden by Michael Roberts)</p>
<p> 2. Classic Cliche    5-4 favourite (Frankie Dettori)</p>
<p> 3. Double Eclipse   12-1	     (Jason Weaver)</p>
<p>10 ran.</p>
<p>Distances: One and a half lengths, half a length.</p>
<p>Winner owned by Rod Huggins and trained in England by Mark</p>
<p>Johnston.</p>
<p>Value to winning owner: 38,700 pounds ($63,200)</p>
</text>
